[[:db/cas 17592186059980 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0-6 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0-6 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186059982 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(Z) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ {y}^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}-y\\cdot {y}^{2} \\\\  & =x-{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(Z) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ {y}^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}-y\\cdot {y}^{2} \\\\  & =x-{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186233379 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & 6 \\\\ 2x & x-2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (x-2)-6\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-16x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-32$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-32 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-16x & =-32 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-16x+32 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-8x+16 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 6 \\\\ 2x & x-2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (x-2)-6\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-16x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-32$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-32 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-16x & =-32 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-16x+32 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-8x+16 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186244112 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(X) & =|\\begin{aligned}10 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =10\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =40-(-3) \\\\  & =43\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(X) & =\\begin{vmatrix}10 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =40-(-3) \\\\  & =43\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186244117 :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle |\\begin{aligned}2x & {y}^{2} \\\\ z & -3\\end{aligned}|=\n$$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}2x & {y}^{2} \\\\ z & -3\\end{vmatrix}=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186244117 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2x & {y}^{2} \\\\ z & -3\\end{aligned}| & =2x\\cdot (-3)-{y}^{2}\\cdot z \\\\  & =-6x-{y}^{2}z\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vma