2\\cdot 3-w\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nSince $det(M)=2$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =2 \\\\ 6-4w & =2 \\\\ -4w & =2-6 \\\\ -4w & =-4 \\\\ w & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-w\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nSince $det(M)=2$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =2 \\\\ 6-4w & =2 \\\\ -4w & =2-6 \\\\ -4w & =-4 \\\\ w & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262796 :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle |\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}|=\n$$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}5 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{vmatrix}=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262796 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}| & =5\\cdot 7-(-9)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =35-27 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{vmatrix} & =5\\cdot 7-(-9)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =35-27 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262797 :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|=\n$$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262797 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}| & =-1\\cdot 5-(-10)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-5-20 \\\\  & =-25\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & =-1\\cdot 5-(-10)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-5-20 \\\\  & =-25\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262800 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}-x & -2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & 5y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-x\\cdot 5y-(-2y)\\cdot \\frac{x}{2} \\\\  & =-5xy+xy \\\\  & =-4xy\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-x & -2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & 5y\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-x\\cdot 5y-(-2y)\\cdot \\frac{x}{2} \\\\  & =-5xy+xy \\\\  & =-4xy\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262802 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & y \\\\ -5 & xy\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2x\\cdot xy-y\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y+5y \\\\  & =y(2{x}^{2}+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2x & y \\\\ -5 & xy\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot xy-y\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y+5y \\\\  & =y(2{x}^{2}+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262803 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(U) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 2k & -k+2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-k+2)-(-5)\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =7k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-1$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-1 \\\\ 7k+6 & =-1 \\\\ 7k & =-1-6 \\\\ 7k & =-7 \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(U) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 2k & -k+2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-k+2)-(-5)\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =7k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-1$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-1 \\\\ 7k+6 & =-1 \\\\ 7k & =-1-6 \\\\ 7k & =-7 \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262804 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}v & 2v \\\\ 2 & v+8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot (v+8)-2v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={v}^{2}+4v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(T)=-4$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v+4 & =0 \\\\ (v+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ v & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =\\begin{vmatrix}v & 2v \\\\ 2 & v+8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =v\\cdot (v+8)-2v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={v}^{2}+4v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(T)=-4$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v+4 & =0 \\\\ (v+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ v & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262805 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =|\\begin{aligned}r-3 & r \\\\ 3 & r\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(r-3)\\cdot r-r\\cdot 3 \\\\  & ={r}^{2}-6r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(P)=-9$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =-9 \\\\ {r}^{2}-6r & =-9 \\\\ {r}^{2}-6r+9 & =0 \\\\ (r-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ r & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =\\begin{vmatrix}r-3 & r \\\\ 3 & r\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(r-3)\\cdot r-r\\cdot 3 \\\\  & ={r}^{2}-6r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(P)=-9$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =-9 \\\\ {r}^{2}-6r & =-9 \\\\ {r}^{2}-6r+9 & =0 \\\\ (r-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ r & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262806 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}5-p & p \\\\ 3 & p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5-p)\\cdot p-p\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-{p}^{2}+2p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(B)=1$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1 \\\\ -{p}^{2}+2p & =1 \\\\ -{p}^{2}+2p-1 & =0 \\\\ {p}^{2}-2p+1 & =0 \\\\ (p-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\begin{vmatrix}5-p & p \\\\ 3 & p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(5-p)\\cdot p-p\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-{p}^{2}+2p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(B)=1$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1 \\\\ -{p}^{2}+2p & =1 \\\\ -{p}^{2}+2p-1 & =0 \\\\ {p}^{2}-2p+1 & =0 \\\\ (p-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186262807 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3y & y \\\\ 3 & y-5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3y\\cdot (y-5)-y\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-18y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=-27$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y+27 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3y & y \\\\ 3 & y-5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3y\\cdot (y-5)-y\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-18y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=-27$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y+27 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186292870 :question/problem "Evaluate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & y \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|=\n$$\n {{field-1}}" "Evaluate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & y \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{vmatrix}=\n$$\n {{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186292870 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & y \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}-y\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & y \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{vmatrix} & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}-y\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186292872 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & k \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 6-k\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(C)=-14$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-14 \\\\ 6-4k & =-14 \\\\ -4k & =-14-6 \\\\ -4k & =-20 \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & k \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 6-k\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(C)=-14$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-14 \\\\ 6-4k & =-14 \\\\ -4k & =-14-6 \\\\ -4k & =-20 \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186292873 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3+p & 4p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5-p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3+p)(5-p)-(4p-{p}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15-3p+5p-{p}^{2}-4p+{p}^{2} \\\\  & =15-2p-\\cancel{{p}^{2}}+\\cancel{{p}^{2}} \\\\  & =15-2p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $det(A)=7$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =7 \\\\ 15-2p & =7 \\\\ -2p & =-8 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3+p & 4p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5-p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3+p)(5-p)-(4p-{p}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15-3p+5p-{p}^{2}-4p+{p}^{2} \\\\  & =15-2p-\\cancel{{p}^{2}}+\\cancel{{p}^{2}} \\\\  & =15-2p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $det(A)=7$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =7 \\\\ 15-2p & =7 \\\\ -2p & =-8 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299591 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(8)(4)-(-5)(3) \\\\  & =32+15 \\\\  & =47.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =\\begin{vmatrix}8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(8)(4)-(-5)(3) \\\\  & =32+15 \\\\  & =47.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299592 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2)(3)-(4)(1) \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2)(3)-(4)(1) \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299593 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(6)(7)-(-2)(5) \\\\  & =42+10 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =\\begin{vmatrix}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(6)(7)-(-2)(5) \\\\  & =42+10 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299596 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{2}{5} & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299597 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(E) & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4} & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-10 \\\\  & =-\\frac{37}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(E) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-\\frac{3}{4} & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-10 \\\\  & =-\\frac{37}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299598 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}3x & 2y \\\\ -5 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3x\\cdot x-2y\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+10y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3x & 2y \\\\ -5 & x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3x\\cdot x-2y\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+10y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299599 :question/problem "Evaluate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}|=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{vmatrix}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299599 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}| & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}-y\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{vmatrix} & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}-y\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299600 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5-m\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =10-3m.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-11,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-11 \\\\ 10-3m & =-11 \\\\ -3m & =-21 \\\\ m & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5-m\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =10-3m.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-11,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-11 \\\\ 10-3m & =-11 \\\\ -3m & =-21 \\\\ m & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299601 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =|\\begin{aligned}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1+r)\\cdot 4-(2-r)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =4+4r+10-5r \\\\  & =14-r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-6 \\\\ 14-r & =-6 \\\\ -r & =-20 \\\\ r & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1+r)\\cdot 4-(2-r)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =4+4r+10-5r \\\\  & =14-r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-6 \\\\ 14-r & =-6 \\\\ -r & =-20 \\\\ r & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299602 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3+s)(3-s)-2s(-4) \\\\  & =9-{s}^{2}+8s \\\\  & =-{s}^{2}+8s+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s+9 & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s-16 & =0 \\\\ {s}^{2}-8s+16 & =0 \\\\ (s-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ s & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3+s)(3-s)-2s(-4) \\\\  & =9-{s}^{2}+8s \\\\  & =-{s}^{2}+8s+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s+9 & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s-16 & =0 \\\\ {s}^{2}-8s+16 & =0 \\\\ (s-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ s & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186335990 :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle |\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}|=\n$$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{vmatrix}=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186335990 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}| & =3\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (-\\sqrt{x})-{z}^{2}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =-3x-2y{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{vmatrix} & =3\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (-\\sqrt{x})-{z}^{2}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =-3x-2y{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186335991 :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & 